2. Source repository
--------------------

The Git repository contains no Tesseract executable, no OCR model files and no
Python wheels. Dependencies are pinned by hash in packaging/*.txt and
packaging/profiles/*.txt. Tesseract model sources and hashes are recorded in
src/desktop_app/data/ocr-four-languages.json (four languages) and
src/desktop_app/data/ocr-models.json (legacy two-language entry).


3. Base package (packaging/base.spec, Windows)
----------------------------------------------

Python runtime packages: the 38-package Windows base runtime lock
(packaging/profiles/base-windows-runtime.txt), including PySide6-Essentials
6.12.0 / shiboken6 (Qt for Python; LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR
GPL-3.0-only per package metadata), Magika and its CPU ONNX Runtime
dependency. Notices actually collected from the installed packages are placed
in desktop_app/data/licenses inside the package and are reachable through
Help / Third-party licenses.

CPython: the build interpreter's runtime DLLs and standard library are
bundled; its LICENSE.txt is copied to
desktop_app/data/licenses/python-runtime/LICENSE.txt.

PyInstaller bootloader: the original PyInstaller license is copied to
desktop_app/data/licenses/bootloader.

Bundled Tesseract OCR engine: the Windows base package DOES include a
tesseract.exe. It is built in CI from pinned source archives recorded in
packaging/native/minimal-windows.json: Tesseract 5.5.3, Leptonica 1.87.0,
libpng 1.6.59 and zlib 1.4, statically linked with an LLVM/MinGW-w64
toolchain. Original license texts for these and for the toolchain runtime
libraries are preserved in packaging/native/minimal-notices and copied to
desktop_app/data/native/notices.

Bundled OCR models: tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast, commit
87416418657359cb625c412a48b6e1d6d41c29bd, Apache-2.0. The base package
includes chi_tra, eng, jpn and kor traineddata plus the official LICENSE in
desktop_app/data/native/tessdata; every file is checked against the pinned
SHA-256 values.

Open items for this profile: Qt (LGPL) relinking/corresponding-source
obligations, Microsoft Universal CRT / Visual C++ runtime redistribution,
OpenSSL and other libraries collected from the build machine, per-file
attribution of CPython's bundled third-party components, and a member-level
inventory of the Python archive. See docs/source-classification.md.


4. Optional CPU OCR component (packaging/ocr-worker.spec, Windows)
------------------------------------------------------------------

Experimental optional OCR: rapidocr-onnxruntime 1.4.4. Package metadata
declares Apache-2.0. Its bundled PP-OCR models are checked against SHA-256
values in src/desktop_app/onnx_ocr.py. Installed artifacts come from PyPI with
TLS and the hashed lock packaging/profiles/cpu-windows-build.txt (24
packages; this lock describes the build environment, not a runtime SBOM).
Collected notices are placed in worker-assets inside the component package,
which also carries its own NOTICE.txt. This component contains no Qt or
Tesseract binaries; it only carries copies of license texts from the
application's notice inventory.

Open items for this profile: runtime/model redistribution review for
rapidocr-onnxruntime, ONNX Runtime and OpenCV, Microsoft runtime
redistribution, and the same CPython/archive items as the base package.


5. Legacy development build (packaging/desktop.spec, manual workflow)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The earlier all-in-one development build uses the 58-package Windows lock
(packaging/requirements-windows.txt), a superset that includes build and test
dependencies. Its notice inventory, original notices and pinned supplemental
sources are in src/desktop_app/data/licenses/windows. In this build the
Tesseract executable is external and is not bundled, and OCR models are
downloaded separately with SHA-256 verification. It is not the delivery
pipeline for the base package.


6. Status
---------

No profile has passed final redistribution review. Windows native-binary
audit, Qt redistribution obligations and the application license remain
release gates; no final distribution compliance claim is made.
